        <body>
            <div xml:id="d80-a3">

                <pb facs="0746" n="734" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv06/pg734"/>

                <head>Appendix III to CF–96</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">German Peace
                            Delegation</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Versailles</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-27">June 27, 1919</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">[<hi rendition="#italic">The President of the German
                        Delegation</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Von Haniel</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the President of the Peace Conference</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Clemenceau</hi>)]</p>
                <p rendition="#center">Translation</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">No. 138</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Imperial Minister for Foreign Affairs
                    has instructed me to inform Your Excellency as follows:— <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The German Government gathers from the Note of the 16th [<hi
                                rendition="#italic">21st</hi>] instant<anchor n="11" xml:id="d80-f1"
                            /> that the Allied and Associated Governments consider also as binding
                            those promises contained in their memorandum of the 16th instant,<anchor
                                n="12" xml:id="d80-f2"/> which were not specially noted in the
                            provisions of the Treaty of Peace. In order to avoid misunderstanding it
                            has no objection to some of those promises being laid down in a final
                            Protocol, as proposed in the Note of the 21st instant.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Von Haniel</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
